Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: runxmlconf.c
Line: 237
Function: xmlconfTestNotNSWF
Bug type: null-pointer-dereference
CWE: CWE-476
Explanation: xmlNewParserCtxt() can return NULL on allocation failure. The returned pointer is used immediately in xmlCtxtSetErrorHandler(ctxt, ...) and later in xmlCtxtReadFile(ctxt, ...), causing a NULL dereference if allocation fails.

Source context:
```c
